Expanded story:
Amy was stirring eggs when the front door creaked open. “Will!” she shouted as a groaning zombie pressed against the knob. She grabbed Will’s small hand and tugged Amber to the closet, sealing it behind them. With kids safe, she sprinted back into the kitchen, heart pounding like a drum.

She slid her pistol from the drawer beneath the stove and drew a katana from the pantry, its blade catching the morning light. Zombies shuffled in through the hallway; one by one Amy fired shots or sliced with steel, each attack echoing off tile. More crawlers surged, heads snapping toward her as she moved like a shadow between them.

The last zombie collapsed into a splatter of flesh and bone. She opened the closet door, pulled Will’s hand back, and carried Amber out to safety.
